  <div class="fcx" aria-label="Axial Fans Manufacturers in Ahmedabad">
<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-duo"><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i></span><h2>What Are Axial Fans?</h2><p>Axial fans move air along the axis of the fan rather than changing the airflow direction through centrifugal action. This makes them appropriate for systems requiring high-volume air movement over large areas or through long ventilation routes.</p><p>Axial fans can be configured with fixed or variable pitch blades, direct-drive or V-belt arrangements, and different casing materials depending on the application. The current range includes impeller diameters from 315 mm to 1600 mm, with an overall airflow range of 1,000 to 180,000 CFM and static pressure up to 100 mm WG.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h2>Tube Axial Fans</h2><p>Tube axial fans are designed to move air parallel to the fan axis and are especially suitable for ventilation systems where airflow needs to travel through ducts or over longer distances.</p><p>The current tube axial range covers 315 mm to 1600 mm diameter, with airflow up to 130,000 CFM. The fans use aluminium alloy aerofoil impellers with fixed and variable pitch options and are available in V-belt or direct-driven configurations.</p><p>The casing is available in heavy-gauge hot-dip galvanized steel or SS304, providing options for different working environments. Tube axial fans can be used in industrial ventilation, tunnels, and other ducted airflow applications.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel" style="grid-column:1/-1"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h2>Vane Axial Fans</h2><p>Vane axial fans contain stationary guide vanes downstream of the impeller. These guide vanes help recover rotational swirl and convert it into useful static pressure, supporting aerodynamic performance and energy efficiency.</p><p>The current range offers high overall efficiency up to 88%. Motor options include IP55/IP65, Class H configurations, along with fire-rated performance of 300°C for 2 hours.</p><p>Vane axial fans are appropriate for applications such as cooling towers, heat exchangers, industrial HVAC plants, and commercial ventilation systems in which airflow and static pressure both need to be considered.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of Axial Fans</h2><p>Axial fans provide various features for commercial, industrial, and emergency ventilation applications:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Impeller diameter from 315 mm to 1600 mm</li><li>Overall airflow from 1,000 to 180,000 CFM</li><li>Static pressure up to 100 mm WG</li><li>Tube axial and vane axial configurations</li><li>Aluminium alloy aerofoil impellers</li><li>Fixed and variable pitch options</li><li>Direct-drive and V-belt configurations</li><li>Heavy-gauge hot-dip galvanized steel casing</li><li>SS304 casing option</li><li>Guide vanes for vane axial models</li><li>Total efficiency up to 88% for vane axial fans</li><li>IP55/IP65, Class H motor options</li><li>Fire-rated option of 300°C for 2 hours</li><li>Dynamically balanced impellers according to ISO 1940 Grade G2.5</li></ul></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-spec"><table class="fcx-table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Fan Type</th><td>Axial Fan</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Configurations</th><td>Tube Axial / Vane Axial</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Impeller Diameter</th><td>315 mm to 1600 mm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Overall Airflow</th><td>1,000 to 180,000 CFM</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tube Axial Airflow</th><td>Up to 130,000 CFM</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Static Pressure</th><td>Up to 100 mm WG</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Impeller</th><td>Aluminium Alloy Aerofoil</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Blade Type</th><td>Fixed &amp; Variable Pitch</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Drive Options</th><td>Direct Drive / V-Belt</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Casing</th><td>Hot-Dip Galvanized Steel / SS304</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Vane Axial Efficiency</th><td>Up to 88% Total Efficiency</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Motor</th><td>IP55/IP65, Class H</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Fire Rating</th><td>300°C / 2 Hours</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Balancing</th><td>ISO 1940 Grade G2.5</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="fcx-note"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-sliders"></i></span><div><p>The final fan configuration should be selected according to the specified airflow, static pressure, application, temperature, installation arrangement, and site conditions.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Applications of Axial Fans</h2><p><b>Axial Fans in Ahmedabad</b> are appropriate for a wide range of industrial and commercial applications. Common applications include:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>General industrial ventilation</li><li>Factory ventilation</li><li>Cooling towers</li><li>Heat exchangers</li><li>HVAC plant rooms</li><li>Industrial exhaust systems</li><li>Tunnels</li><li>Emergency ventilation</li><li>Commercial HVAC systems</li><li>Long-distance duct ventilation</li><li>Process ventilation</li><li>Large-area air movement</li></ul><p>Ahmedabad and the wider Gujarat industrial belt include GIDC estates around Vatva, Naroda, Changodar, and Sanand. These areas have textile mills, chemical and pharmaceutical plants, engineering units, and automotive industries. Many such facilities operate continuously in a warm and dry climate, making reliable air movement crucial for ventilation and process conditions.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Benefits of Axial Fans</h2></div><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--3"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-gauge-high"></i></span><h3>High Airflow Capacity</h3><p>Axial fans are designed to move large quantities of air, making them appropriate for commercial buildings, ventilation ducts, cooling systems, and other applications requiring high-volume airflow.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h3>Flexible Blade Options</h3><p>Fixed and variable pitch impeller options provide flexibility when selecting the fan for different airflow and system requirements.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-bolt"></i></span><h3>Efficient Air Movement</h3><p>Aerofoil impellers are designed to provide efficient airflow, while vane axial fans use downstream guide vanes to improve static pressure recovery.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-ruler-combined"></i></span><h3>Wide Application Range</h3><p>Tube axial and vane axial configurations allow these fans to be used across industrial ventilation, HVAC, cooling towers, heat exchangers, tunnels, and emergency ventilation.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fire"></i></span><h3>Fire-Rated Options</h3><p>For applications requiring emergency smoke or high-temperature ventilation, fire-rated configurations are available with 300°C operation for 2 hours.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Axial Fans Suppliers in Ahmedabad</h2><p>When selecting <b>Axial Fans Suppliers in Ahmedabad</b>, it is critical to provide complete technical details before finalizing the fan. Required airflow, static pressure, temperature, duct arrangement, installation space, and operating environment can all affect the right configuration.</p><p>For industrial projects around Ahmedabad, the fan can be required for general ventilation, cooling towers, heat exchangers, HVAC plant rooms, or industrial exhaust systems. The fan should therefore be selected according to the actual operating requirements instead of using the same configuration for each application.</p></div><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Axial Fans Manufacturer in India</h2><p>For projects looking for an <b>Axial Fans Manufacturer in India</b>, proper technical sizing is vital for achieving the required airflow and pressure performance. Tube axial and vane axial configurations may be selected according to the application and system design.</p><p>The production facility is located in Neemrana, Rajasthan. Each unit is chosen according to the required airflow, static pressure, and site conditions, with completed equipment dispatched to Ahmedabad and other locations across India. Technical sizing and product data may be reviewed before ordering.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>How to Choose the Right Axial Fan</h2><p>Before choosing an axial fan, consider the following factors:</p><ul class="fcx-checks fcx-checks--long"><li><b>Airflow Requirement:</b> Determine the specified CFM for the complete ventilation system.</li><li><b>Static Pressure:</b> Calculate pressure losses through ducts, filters, dampers, grilles, and other components.</li><li><b>Fan Type:</b> Select tube axial or vane axial according to the application.</li><li><b>Fan Diameter:</b> Choose an appropriate impeller size based on airflow and installation area.</li><li><b>Blade Configuration:</b> Consider fixed or variable pitch requirements.</li><li><b>Drive Arrangement:</b> Select direct-drive or V-belt configuration as required.</li><li><b>Temperature:</b> Check whether a standard or fire-rated configuration is needed.</li><li><b>Casing Material:</b> Consider galvanized steel or SS304 according to the operating environment.</li><li><b>Installation Conditions:</b> Review available space, duct arrangement, access, and maintenance requirements.</li></ul></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What are axial fans used for?</summary><p>Axial fans are used for high-volume air movement in industrial ventilation, cooling towers, heat exchangers, HVAC plant rooms, tunnels, and emergency ventilation systems.</p></details><details><summary>What sizes of axial fans are available?</summary><p>The current range covers 315 mm to 1600 mm impeller diameter.</p></details><details><summary>What is the airflow capacity of axial fans?</summary><p>The overall airflow range is 1,000 to 180,000 CFM, while tube axial fans offer airflow up to 130,000 CFM.</p></details><details><summary>What is the difference between tube axial and vane axial fans?</summary><p>Tube axial fans move air parallel to the fan axis and are appropriate for ducted and long-distance airflow applications. Vane axial fans use downstream guide vanes to recover swirl and improve static pressure performance.</p></details><details><summary>Are fire-rated axial fans available?</summary><p>Yes. The current range includes fire-rated configurations with 300°C operation for 2 hours, depending on the chosen model and application.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Axial fans offer an effective solution for applications requiring high-volume and reliable air movement. With tube axial and vane axial configurations, different impeller sizes, fixed and variable pitch options, and fire-rated models, they can be tailored to a wide range of commercial and industrial ventilation requirements.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. provides axial fan solutions for Ahmedabad and other places across India, with selection based on airflow, static pressure, application, temperature rating, and location conditions. Technical requirements can be reviewed before ordering to identify a suitable axial fan configuration for the project.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
